(4916374, 712281, 72096, '<td valign="top">I am one of your 10''s.  I love this shot.  I cannot believe that you ended up 20th.  I cannot understand that people can see a shot like this and vote anything below 6.  In any case, congratulations for your obvious efforts.</td>', 'I am one of your 10''s.  I love this shot.  I cannot believe that you ended up 20th.  I cannot understand that people can see a shot like this and vote anything below 6.  In any case, congratulations for your obvious efforts.', '2008-08-27 20:38:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(4916376, 710459, 77196, '<td valign="top">OK... She who complains about a 5.9... <br/>Possible vote losers: Too busy (gingham checks and polka dots for table / background), hot spots on pool ball, main subject not purple, bottom of the ball cropped off, visible gap between background and table cloths on right side, black spots on top crown points. I''m also trying to figure out if the crown is too tall - out of scale with the frog / ball - not sure about that. FWIW. <br/>Now for my wife: Nothing special about the picture (I asked her - a frog with a crown - nothing special?), too busy - thinks that a white table / background would''ve made the purple ball / frog pop, also thought the frog''s face looked a bit OOF. <br/> <br/>Subjectively - it makes me smile. It also gives me visions of trying to pose the frog, set the flash, focus, and getting ready to snap, when the frog is done and gives a little hop and goes on his/her merry way.<br/> <br/>I enjoy so many of your photos (your hubby too), and I smile when I see either of you ribbon. <br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-08-27 19:42:09.</i></td>', 'OK... She who complains about a 5.9... Possible vote losers: Too busy (gingham checks and polka dots for table / background), hot spots on pool ball, main subject not purple, bottom of the ball cropped off, visible gap between background and table cloths on right side, black spots on top crown points. I''m also trying to figure out if the crown is too tall - out of scale with the frog / ball - not sure about that. FWIW. Now for my wife: Nothing special about the picture (I asked her - a frog with a crown - nothing special?), too busy - thinks that a white table / background would''ve made the purple ball / frog pop, also thought the frog''s face looked a bit OOF.  Subjectively - it makes me smile. It also gives me visions of trying to pose the frog, set the flash, focus, and getting ready to snap, when the frog is done and gives a little hop and goes on his/her merry way. I enjoy so many of your photos (your hubby too), and I smile when I see either of you ribbon. ', '2008-08-27 20:40:17.000000', '2008-08-27 20:42:09.000000', 0),
(4916383, 711366, 45475, '<td valign="top">Even though your flash was set low, tell-tale signs of direct flash are still visible. Shine on the nose and around the mouth, cheek and the eyes. There''s also a harsh shadow on the neck under the chin. That all adds up to making the image look washed out/snap-shotty.<br/> <br/>You''ve also lost texture in the hair, which is a little disappointing. Neat Image may have been the culprit there.<br/> <br/><img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=88204" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">choltmeier</a>''s advice is sound, use natural light. Or even try diffusing/bouncing the flash.</td>', 'Even though your flash was set low, tell-tale signs of direct flash are still visible. Shine on the nose and around the mouth, cheek and the eyes. There''s also a harsh shadow on the neck under the chin. That all adds up to making the image look washed out/snap-shotty. You''ve also lost texture in the hair, which is a little disappointing. Neat Image may have been the culprit there.  choltmeier''s advice is sound, use natural light. Or even try diffusing/bouncing the flash.', '2008-08-27 20:42:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(4916423, 712270, 72096, '<td valign="top">You get an A+ for composition.  Personally, I would have preferred a sharper image instead of this soft focus.  You defineately deserved the covetted "6"+ average for this image.  What fool gave you a 2??  I look forward to seeing your future entries.</td>', 'You get an A+ for composition.  Personally, I would have preferred a sharper image instead of this soft focus.  You defineately deserved the covetted "6"+ average for this image.  What fool gave you a 2??  I look forward to seeing your future entries.', '2008-08-27 21:01:25.000000', NULL, 0),
